  "question": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{N}_{2}$ and $\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ are converted into mono anions, $\\mathrm{N}_{2}^{-}$ and $\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{-}$ respectively. Which of the following statements is wrong ?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\operatorname{In} \\mathrm{N}_{2}$, the $\\mathrm{N}-\\mathrm{N}$ bond weakens",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "In $\\mathrm{O}_{2}$, the $\\mathrm{O}-\\mathrm{O}$ bond order increases",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "In $\\mathrm{O}_{2},$ bond length decreases",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{N}_{2}^{-}$ becomes diamagnetic",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "We know that in $\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ bond, the order is 2 and in $\\mathrm{O}_{2}^{-}$ bond, the order is 1.5 . Therefore the wrong statements is (b)."
  }
